<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Janata Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1977">1977</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Janata Party was an Indian political party formed in 1977 by the merger of opposition groups, from socialists to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> nationalist Jana Sangh, to fight <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indira-gandhi">Indira Gandhi</a> after the Emergency. It won the general election of March 1977 and formed the first national government not led by the Congress, with Morarji Desai as prime minister. Divided by rivalries, it broke apart in 1979 and lost the 1980 election.</p></div>
